FP","urlSource":"images/ohiolink1.png"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":73,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This search for theses and dissertations submitted after 2020 by students matriculating from The Ohio State University’s Neuroscience Graduate Studies Program yields 39 records, with 20 results showing per page. The search url does not include any visible search parameters or facets, and it remains unchanged even when navigating to the second page of results.","position":{"start":{"line":73,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"key":"uyXKQSvXs6"}],"key":"NIyEvDoq9A"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"https://etd.ohiolink.edu/acprod/odb_etd/r/etd/search/search-results?p1001_advanced=1&clear=0,1001","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"key":"tSA32lez7m"}],"key":"cOtV4ClLfU"}],"class":"dropdown","key":"KdvbVUpMHj"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The OhioLINK ","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"key":"tBQ8MJauPF"},{"type":"link","url":"https://etd.ohiolink.edu/acprod/odb_etd/r/etd/search/1?clear=0,1,5,10,20,21,1001","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electronic Theses and Dissertations Center","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"key":"YocVV888xb"}],"urlSource":"https://etd.ohiolink.edu/acprod/odb_etd/r/etd/search/1?clear=0,1,5,10,20,21,1001","key":"Ey0xVzbn4t"},{"type":"text","value":" operates as a ","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"key":"G8TuhQAQBC"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"dynamic website","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"key":"Ren57AadRr"}],"key":"oPu5RlJdt5"},{"type":"text","value":". While the page layout - including the headers, footers, and general structure -- is built into the static HTML, the actual search results are dynamically retrieved from a server and injected into this framework.","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"key":"ld8ok8ealT"}],"key":"q6TTD4xiQM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you inspect the page using Developer Tools, you’ll find that each search result is rendered within the ","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"c4FrRYV8qh"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<div class=\"t-SearchResults-content\">","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"CKZtuqSQAj"},{"type":"text","value":" element. This structure allows the OhioLINK ETD to update content without reloading the entire page.","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"kO4uISwAsS"}],"key":"tROH36voib"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"<div class=\"t-SearchResults-content\">\n            <h3 class=\"t-SearchResults-title\">\n                1. <span class=\"t-SearchResults-author\">Mackey-Alfonso, Sabrina</span>\n                <a href=\"/acprod/odb_etd/r/etd/search/10?p10_accession_num=osu1744894008278402&amp;clear=10&amp;session=10473290292427\">Short-term High Fat Diet Accelerates Synaptic and Memory Deficits via Neuroinflammatory Mechanisms in an Alzheimer's Disease Mouse Model</a>\n            </h3>\n            <div class=\"t-SearchResults-info\">\n              <p class=\"t-SearchResults-degree\">\n                  Doctor of Philosophy, The Ohio State University, 2025, Neuroscience Graduate Studies Program\n              </p>\n              <p class=\"t-SearchResults-desc hide-class\"><div style=\"overflow: hidden; height: 40px;\">Alzheimer's Disease (AD) is a neurodegenerative disease characterized by profound memory impairments, synaptic loss, neuroinflammation, and hallmark pathological markers. High-fat diet (HFD) consumption increases the risk of developing AD even after controlling for metabolic syndrome, pointing to a role of the diet itself in increasing risk. In AD, the complement system, an arm of the immune system which normally tags redundant or damaged synapses for pruning, becomes pathologically overactivated leading to tagging of healthy synapses. While the unhealthy diet to AD link is strong, the underlying mechanisms are not well understood in part due to confounding variables associated with long-term HFD which can independently influence the brain. Therefore, we experimented with a short-term diet regimen to isolate the diet's impact on brain function without causing changes in metabolic markers.\nThis project investigated potential mechanisms underlying cognitive impairments evoked by short-term diet consumption using the 3xTg-AD model. In chapter 1 we discuss the link between HFD and AD and outline the current findings and hypothesis regarding of relevant mechanisms. In chapter 2 we characterize the effect of short-term HFD on 1) memory, 2) neuroinflammation including complement, 3) AD pathology markers, 4) synaptic markers, and 5) in vitro microglial synaptic phagocytosis in the 3xTg-AD mouse model. In chapter 3 we analyze two potential mechanisms underlying HFD-mediated AD vulnerability: toll-like receptor 4 (TLR4)-evoked neuroinflammation and complement system activation. Finally, in chapter 4 we validate the absence of glucose modifications as an effect of the diet and drug treatment, explore potential mitochondrial mechanisms in the hippocampus, and evaluate the diet's impact on the pre-frontal cortex (PFC).\nFollowing the consumption of either standard chow or HFD, 3xTg-AD mice exhibited impaired long-term memory performance which was associated with increased level (open full item for complete abstract)</div> <a href=\"#\" data-ctrl=\"\" class=\"\">... <em>More</em></a></p>\n              <span class=\"t-SearchResults-misc\"><b>Committee:</b> Ruth Barrientos (Advisor); Benedetta Leuner (Committee Member); Nikki Kokiko-Cochran (Committee Member); Harry Fu (Committee Member)</span>\n              <span class=\"t-SearchResults-misc\"><b>Subjects:</b> Neurosciences</span>\n              <!-- span class=\"t-SearchResults-misc\">Score: 100</span -->\n            </div>\n        </div>","key":"cRnHAb30nL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you try to scrape your search results using ","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"key":"TDQN4BXoRy"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"requests","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"key":"EoJhWRKfqr"}],"key":"AOsrJAuKro"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"key":"va8tu0qEQi"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"BeautifulSoup","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"key":"OgAISVMNjw"}],"key":"iqrOAYNA5q"},{"type":"text","value":", however, you will quickly realize that the retrieved page only includes the static HTML shell, none of the dynamically loaded search results are included. This happens because the content is rendered via JavaScript after the initial page load.","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"key":"CnpGz38CdF"}],"key":"Gkg9VaCvKP"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":105,"column":1},"end":{"line"